in favor signify by saying I Any opposed Seeing that that resolution is unanimous the recommendation in the finance committee at the next meeting of the governing body will be to adopt Next item number 20 resolution reappropriating the fiscal year 2026 budget of the city of Cheyenne according to the provisions of Wyoming state statutes 16-4-112 and 16-4-113 Staff report Good afternoon chairman members of the finance committee Uh my name is Robin Lman I'm the city treasurer Thank you for the opportunity to provide some additional information on the final reappropriation for last fiscal year The memo I provided contains the full details but I want to highlight the key points particularly those affecting the general fund reserves and

the self- insurance fund The total reappropriation request is approximately $5 million of that amount 1,631,979 is being requested from general fund reserves The remaining approximately 3.3 million is supported by additional revenue and reserves from our other funds So those requests do not use general fund reserves The majority of the general fund requests reflects the way we manage our budget throughout the year As I have explained in the past there are certain costs that are very difficult or impossible to accurately predict when we predict prepare the budget more than a year in advance These include employee sick and vacation vac payouts for when an employee leaves the city accident related costs vandalism and theft utilities fleet fuel parts and

labor Rather than overbudgeting these items in every department and tying up funds that may not be needed we budget them based on the best information available and make necessary adjustments at year end We also do not require departments to reduce their other operating expenditures to cover costs that they really have very little control over For fiscal year 2026 we are requesting approximately 97,000 for accident and damage claims 120,000 for natural gas and electricity increases 142,000 for fleet cost increases 172,000 for employee sick and vacation payouts and approximately 36,000 for vandalism and theft expenses There are also several larger more specific general fund requests that I want to point out We are requesting 149,000 for higher than anticipated inmate housing costs at the Larmy County Detention Center as well as an approximately 378,000 for the combined communication center The communication center increase was primarily due to several previously hard to fill vacate vacant positions being filled during the year We are also requesting approximately 155,000 for the municipal court and

former senior center renovation design contract that was previously approved by the governing body and $350,000 for the purchase of the property at 803 West 16th Street which was previously approved by the governing body as well I also want to provide some context on the self- insurance fund request because the $2.7 million reappropriation is a very large number Since the city is self-insured we essentially act as our own health insurance company The premiums paid by the city and our employees go into this fund and we use those dollars to pay our employees health care claim expenses Fiscal year 2026 was a particularly high claims year Our benefit consultant has advised us that based on their experience the self insurance their self-funded plan can generally expect a more difficult claims year every five years We've had our plan for four years now and

we've had very good claims experience in fiscal years 23 24 and 25 We also purchase stop-loss insurance to protect the city when claims become exceptionally high It protects us both when an individual has extremely high medical expenses and when the city's claims as a whole becomes exceptionally high For the overall plan the insurance begins paying when our claims reach 100% of an the established threshold At the end of fiscal year 26 we were still below that threshold at 87% The goal is 80% or lower which is based on the Affordable Care Act's requirement that 80% of all premiums collected must go to pay for medical care and quality improvement rather than administration overhead and profit It is also important to understand that the 2.7 million reappropriation does not represent a $2.7 million loss to the fund We received approximately 12.2 2 million in revenue during the year and

had 12.9 million in expenses So the self- insurance fund decreased approximately by 690,000 for the entire fiscal year The fund ended June 30th with a reserve of approximately $3.7 million For context when we began the self- insurance fund on July 1st of 2022 we started with approximately 1.4 million in reserves As far as how much we should maintain in reserves our benefits consultant has recommended a minimum of six months of claim expenses with 12 months being the ideal target Looking at our claims experience over the four years we have been self-insured we have averaged approximately 9.3 million in claims annually Based on that average 6 months would be approximately 4.7 million and 12 months would be approximately 9.3 million As I said we ended fiscal year 26 with approximately 3.7 million which represents just under five months of average claims expenses So

our first goal is to maintain at that least at least at the six-month level and over time continue toward the longer term reserve level recommended by our benefits consultant This is why we build reserves in the first place They allow us to absorb a higher claims year like fiscal year 2026 without immediately having to make significant changes to employee benefits or contributions In fact that was the reason for establishing the reserve target when we first became self-insured You may also recall through the fiscal year 27 budget process the governing body approved a $1 million transfer from general fund reserves to the self- insurance fund That $1 million is not included in the $3.7 million balance that I just provided Once that transfer is included we began fiscal year 27 with the approximately 4.7 million in reserves which puts us exactly at our six-month minimum target reserve level target based on the four years of average claims experience I am happy to answer any questions you may have on these requests and

