chair My name is Ryan Anderson battalion chief with Shine Fire Rescue The proposal for you is for the purchase of 90 sets of firefighting turnout gear Each set includes uh an ensemble of a coat and pants The quote for 90 sets totals $331,49160 This was a successful proposition within the last six penny One thing I want to bring to your attention I'd like you guys to refer to quotes that were dated 918 And I'll discuss the substitution later on in this presentation Uh these sets are manufactured by Globe MSA The uh sole supplier of Globe MSA for this region is LN Curtis The Soul Source acquisition has been approved by purchasing manager TJ Bartlebort and

the Soul Source letter is included in the documentation provided Um Ellen Curtis and Globe have uh committed to a 90 business day delivery time once the order is placed Uh just a little bit of background for your information NFPA 19 uh70 the National Fire Protection Association uh certifies structural turnout gear for 10 years Once that 10-year um limit is reached it can be utilized for non-live fire training We typically rotate that older gear out to our fire academy and let our recruits use and abuse it if you will dragging it along the ground uh and so forth but it can't be used in live fire situations Um per our CLA with the city um each Shine firefighter is issued two sets of turnout gear Second sets necessary to due to the increased risks of exposure to carcinogenic agents that contaminate gear after a structure fire The clean set is back at their stations and

can be placed into service immediately uh upon return And while the contaminated set is properly decontaminated and dried inhouse by our personnel this therefore reduces firefighter downtime and provides them the proper PPE that they need almost instantaneously So the turnout gear we're discussing uh in this purchase will replace an original set that was u bought in 2016 and I'll refer to it as the orange trim sets Um the reason we do that we alternate between yellow trim and orange trim so we can best identify our primary set and our backup set So that way a fire officer on scene can wonder why his firefighter has been in his backup set for an extended period of time Is it out of service due to repair Is there something else going on Um

the substitution that I referenced earlier um we initially were pursuing their um mid highlevel brand of globe gear called Extreme Pro um and had proceeded through the sizing process We actually just received the um trial sets about a month ago Uh unfortunately once we got them we found there was a vast difference in the sizing I'm already a big guy and my coat fit me like a circus tent Um kind of what we came to the conclusion was is new isn't always better We wanted to go back to what we know and what we really enjoy and what we've been told is the best gear guys have worn online And so um Globe and Ellen Curtis were gracious enough to give us a promotional pricing for the G Extreme 3.0 compared to the Pro So

that's what the substitute is is as it relates to Um there's no price change It's for the 90 sets It's literally just a change in description to make sure that we're providing our guys with the gear that they like that they know that we're familiar with Um like I said new isn't always better We're finding through this So I appreciate your uh consideration I'm happy to answer any questions Any comments or questions for um Thank you Mr Chairman Through you um are are these uh and thank you for your presentation Chief Um are these are these sized individuals or they Yes sir So um what we'll do and and actually that's kind of another fortunate thing with us going back to the 3.0 I know Um

